# Chinese Source Rules

## Encoding and Script

- UTF-8; prefer Traditional (繁體)
- If source uses Simplified, add YAML frontmatter: `script: simplified`
- Note variant characters: `（異體：X）` in translator notes, not inline in source unless correcting

## Punctuation

Source bodies use **ASCII punctuation only** — normalize when creating or editing (see `docs/2. So tay bien tap.md` §1.2.2).

**Order:** multi-char marks first (`──`, `——`, `......`, `……`) → strip `《》` → single-character swaps.

| From | To |
|------|-----|
| `……` / `......` | `[...]` |
| `──` / `——` | `–` |
| `《` / `》` | *(remove; keep inner text)* |
| `，` / `、` | `,` |
| `。` / `．` | `.` |
| `？` | `?` |
| `！` | `!` |
| `；` | `;` |
| `：` | `:` |
| `（` / `）` | `(` / `)` |
| `「` / `」` | `"` |
| `『` / `』` | `'` |
| `“` / `”` | `"` |
| `‘` / `’` | `'` |
| `·` | `–` |

**Keep:** `□`, `[ ]`, `< >`, `~`. No spaces between Chinese characters.

## Structure

- One file per chapter or logical section
- YAML frontmatter for metadata only (title, series, volume, chapter, edition)
- **Body = plain text** — one paragraph per line where possible for line-aligned translation

Frontmatter template:

```yaml
---
title: "Chapter title in Chinese"
series: avatamsaka
volume: "01"
chapter: "01"
source_edition: "CBETA T09"
---
```

## Segmentation

- Do not merge paragraphs across 段落 breaks
- Preserve `<!-- verse -->` markers if added during segmentation
- Keep 科判 / section titles as **plain-text lines** in the body (same line as in the edition), not as Markdown `#` headings
- Do not translate inside `.zh.md` files

## Editing Source

- OCR fixes only; document in `notes/` or file footer
